// RTE-004: retired path with no successor -> 410 (App Router pages cannot set a status themselves).
const RETIRED = new Set(['/old-product', '/2019-sale']);
if (RETIRED.has(request.nextUrl.pathname)) {
  return new NextResponse('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><title>Gone</title><body><nav><a href="/">Home</a></nav><h1>This page has been removed</h1></body></html>', {
    status: 410,
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'X-Robots-Tag': 'noindex' },
  });
}

Next.js 15/16 App Router. A plain HTML form posting to a route handler: it works without JavaScript, redirects (303) to a thank-you state only after the downstream call succeeded, and answers 502 when delivery fails. Set SITE_URL and FORM_WEBHOOK_URL (your CRM, form provider or mail API; for email use your provider's HTTPS API the same way). The in-memory limiter is per instance: use Redis/Upstash when you run several. Add Cloudflare Turnstile (`cf-turnstile-response`, verified server-side) if bots get past the honeypot.
